    58	\uses{mumford-conv-variety-field}
    59	\begin{proof}
    60	Restrict $f$ to the slice through a chosen $x_0$; this gives the only possible
    61	$g$.  To verify that it works, test the graph of $f$ over an affine
    62	neighbourhood of $z_0$.  Properness of the first projection shows that the
    63	parameters for which the image leaves this neighbourhood form a closed set
    64	disjoint from $y_0$.  Over its complement, regular functions on the complete
    65	fibres are constant, so the graph is the pullback of the graph of $g$.
    66	Equality of morphisms on this dense open and separatedness of $Z$ extend the
    67	identity to all of $X\times Y$; the slice also proves uniqueness.
    68	\end{proof}
