    80	the two pullbacks of $f$.  Their quotient is a morphism from $A\times A$ to
    81	$B$ which is trivial on both coordinate axes.  Applying rigidity first in one
    82	variable and then in the other makes this quotient trivial, proving additivity.
    83	The original translation is the unique constant term.
    84	\end{proof}
